 "notes": [
  "generation 1 evaluates the INITIAL population, whose graph the timed first call already compiled, so generation 1 is expected to hit; it is recorded as measured (not warmed up away) and the interesting number is generations 2..N",
  "batch route: ONE merged graph per population structure multiset, so a multi-second first_call_ms is the expected cold cost of the route, recorded as measured and never treated as a defect or retried away",
  "named composition route: the route's own knob spec EVOGP_BATCH_BANDS=auto, EVOGP_BATCH_CHUNK_BANDS=1, EVOGP_BATCH_COMPILE_WORKERS=4 is applied AFTER arms.apply_arm_env cleared the table and wrote the arm's own knobs, so protocol.route_knobs states which layer set each variable",
  "batch route: the content blocks (first_call / sr_fitness / generations[i] / summary) price the plan-key REUSE surface, not the compile itself. The identity table is consulted first, so a repeated call on the same Forest object AND the same plan parameters leaves the content table untouched (attempts 0, which is not a content miss); a first call for a NEW plan shape is an identity miss even on an unchanged object, so it does probe the content table (one attempt, usually a miss that stores the entry), and only a REBUILT-but-equal population can produce a content hit -- which means the merge was served instead of re-decoded, re-traced and re-merged"
 ],
